# Canonical production-source baseline established at 0fafdd4 and block count
# ratcheted after the include-scope audit (2026-08-12).
# Scope: Rust files below src/. Test-only Rust is reported separately.
#
# Increasing a ceiling requires a separately reviewed security rationale.
# Decreases should be committed after an audited cleanup checkpoint so the
# ratchet cannot drift back upward.
# crypt-callable-salt-contracts: three deliberately added native boundary
# blocks (crypt_ra/copy, allocation release, lazy loading/capability), no new unsafe
# functions. Review rationale and full ownership proof: docs/crypt-boundary.md.
# php-heap (2026-09-27): the PHP-tailored global allocator (src/heap) adds
# 83 blocks and 24 unsafe functions: page carving over one reserved mapping,
# per-page intrusive free lists, the lock-free remote-free/ownership protocol,
# page recycling and the GlobalAlloc contract. Invariants and ownership proof:
# docs/php-heap-design.md. The user waived the ceiling for this work.
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_BLOCKS=1710
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_FUNCTIONS=313
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_SAFETY_COMMENTS=58
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_SAFETY_SECTIONS=0
